{
  "title": "Sahifa Sajjadiya 30: For Help in Repaying Debts",
  "data": "اللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِهٖ، وَهَبْ لِيَ الْعَافِيَةَ مِنْ دَيْنٍ تُخْلِقُ بِهٖ وَجْهِي، وَيَحَارُ فِيهِ ذِهْنِي، وَيَتَشَعَّبُ لَهٗ فِكْرِي، وَيَطُولُ بِمُمَارَسَتِهٖ شُغْلِي،\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE WA HAB LIYAL A'AFIYATA MIN DAYNIN TUKHLIQU BIHEE WAJHEE WA YAHAARU FEEHI DHIHNEE WA YATASHA''ABU LAHOO FIKREE WA YATOOLU BIMUMAARASATIHEE SHUGHLEE\nO God, bless Muhammad and his Household and release me from a debt which makes me lose face, confuses my mind, disrupts my thinking, and prolongs my occupation with attending to it!\nوَاَعُوذُ بِكَ يَا رَبِّ مِنْ هَمِّ الدَّيْنِ وَفِكْرِهٖ، وَشُغْلِ الدَّيْنِ وَسَهَرِهٖ، فَصَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِهٖ، وَاَعِذْنِي مِنْهُ، وَاَسْتَجِيرُ بِكَ، يَا رَبِّ، مِنْ ذِلَّتِهٖ فِي الْحَيَاةِ، وَمِنْ تَبِعَتِهٖ بَعْدَ الْوَفَاةِ، فَصَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِهٖ، وَاَجِرْني مِنْهُ بِوُسْعٍ فَاضِلٍ اَوْ كَفَافٍ وَاصِلٍ\nWA A'OODHU BIKA YAA RABBI MIN HAMMID DAYNI WA FIKRIHEE WA SHUGHLID DAYNI WA SAHARIHEE FASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE WA A'IDHNEE MINHU WA ASTAJEERU BIKA YAA RABBI MIN DHILLATIHEE FIL HAYAATI WA MIN TABI'ATIHEE BA'DAL WAFAATI FASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE WA AJIRNEE MINHU BIWUS'IN FAADILIN AW KAFAAFIN WAASIL\nI seek refuge in Thee, my Lord, from worry and thought about debt, from the distraction and sleeplessness of debt; so bless Muhammad and his Household and give me refuge from it! I seek sanctuary in Thee, my Lord, from debt's abasement in life and its ill effects after death, so bless Muhammad and his Household and give me sanctuary from it through a bountiful plenty or a continually arriving sufficiency!\nاللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِهٖ، وَاحْجُبْنِي عَنِ السَّرَفِ وَالِازْدِيَادِ، وَقَوِّمْنِي بِالْبَذْلِ وَالِاقْتِصَادِ، وَعَلِّمْنِي حُسْنَ التَّقْدِيرِ، وَاقْبِضْنِي بِلُطْفِكَ عَنِ التَّبْذِيرِ، وَاَجْرِ مِنْ اَسْبَابِ الْحَلَالِ اَرْزَاقِي، وَوَجِّهْ فِي اَبْوَابِ الْبِرِّ اِنْفَاقِي، وَازْوِ عَنِّي مِنَ الْمَالِ مَا يُحْدِثُ لِي مَخِيلَةً اَوْ تَاَدِّياً اِلَى بَغْيٍ اَوْ مَا اَتَعَقَّبُ مِنْهُ طُغْيَاناً\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE WAHJUBNEE A'NIS SARAFI WAALIZDIYAADI WA QAWWIMNEE BIL BADHLI WAALIQTISAADI WA A'LLIMNEE HUSNAT TAQDEERI WAQBIDNEE BILUTFIKA A'NIT TABDHEERI WA AJRI MIN ASBAABIL HALAALI ARZAAQEE WA WAJJIH FEE ABWAABIL BIRRI INFAAQEE WAZWI A'NNEE MINAL MAALI MAA YUHDITHU LEE MAKHEELATAN AW TA'ADDEEAN ILAA BAGHYIN AW MAA ATA'AQQABU MINHU TUGHYAAN\nO God, bless Muhammad and his Household prevent me from extravagance and excess, put me on the course of generous spending and moderation, teach me excellent distribution, hold me back through Thy gentleness from squandering, allow me to attain my provisions through lawful means, direct my spending toward the gateways of devotion, and take away from me any possession which will bring forth pride in me, lead to insolence, or drag me in its heels to rebellion!\nاللَّهُمَّ حَبِّبْ اِلَيَّ صُحْبَةَ الْفُقَرَاءِ، وَاَعِنِّي عَلَى صُحْبَتِهِمْ بِحُسْنِ الصَّبْرِ\nALLAAHUMMA HABBIB ILAYYA SUHBATAL FUQARAA'I WA A'INNEE A'LAA SUHBATIHIM BIHUSNIS SABR\nO God, make me love the companionship of the poor and help me be their companion with excellent patience!\nوَمَا زَوَيْتَ عَنِّي مِنْ مَتَاعِ الدُّنْيَا الْفَانِيَةِ فَاذْخَرْهُ لِي فِي خَزَائِنِكَ الْبَاقِيَةِ\nWA MAA ZAWAYTA A'NNEE MIN MATAA'ID DUNYAL FAANIYATI FADHKHARHU LEE FEE KHAZAA'INIKAL BAAQIYAH\nWhenever Thou takest away from me the goods of this perishing world, store them for me in Thy abiding treasuries!\nوَاجْعَلْ مَا خَوَّلْتَنِي مِنْ حُطَامِهَا، وَعَجَّلْتَ لِي مِنْ مَتَاعِهَا بُلْغَةً اِلَى جِوَارِكَ وَوُصْلَةً اِلَى قُرْبِكَ وَذَرِيعَةً اِلَى جَنَّتِكَ، اِنَّكَ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيمِ، وَاَنْتَ الْجَوَادُ الْكَرِيمُ\nWAJ'AL MAA KHAWWALTANEE MIN HUTAAMIHAA WA A'JJALTA LEE MIN MATAA'IHAA BULGHATAN ILAA JIWAARIKA WA WUSLATAN ILAA QURBIKA WA DHAREE'ATAN ILAA JANNATIKA INNAKA DHUL FADLIL A'ZEEMI WA ANTAL JAWAADUL KAREEM\nMake this world's broken pieces which Thou hast conferred upon me and its goods which Thou hast quickly granted to me a way to reach Thy neighbourhood, a link to Thy nearness, and a means to Thy Garden! Verily Thou art Possessor of bounty abounding, and Thou art the Munificent, the Generous.",
  "merits": "The thirtieth supplication of al-Sahifah al-Kamilah al-Sajjadiyyah: Imam Zayn al-Abidin (a.s.)'s supplication for help in repaying debts.\n\nEnglish translation by William C. Chittick."
